      "id": "42bbafde-9399-46b4-bf86-c2ed951e0ffd",
      "title": "Market Demand Validation Analysis",
      "category": "Other",
      "subcategory": "Experiments",
      "bodyType": "standard",
      "body": "Analyze [BUSINESS IDEA] for genuine market demand using behavioral economics and Jobs-to-be-Done framework.\n\nDIMENSION 1: The Core Problem\nDefine the specific pain point in 1-2 sentences. Must be an unwanted experience (not a missing feature), occurring at least weekly (B2C) or monthly (B2B), with clear trigger events.\n\nDIMENSION 2: The Person Who Feels It Strongest\nCreate a specific persona: their role/context when the problem occurs, urgency level (1-10), and willingness to pay (have they spent money solving this before?).\n\nDIMENSION 3: The Emotional Reason They Care\nSurface emotion, deeper emotional driver (fear of failure, social status, loss aversion), and intensity rating (Low/Medium/High/Extreme). Flag \"mild inconvenience\" as weak demand.\n\nDIMENSION 4: Real-World Proof\nCite at least 2: search volume/keywords, compensating behaviors, community discussions (Reddit/forums), current spending patterns.\n\nDIMENSION 5: Current Solutions & Workarounds\nMap direct competitors, indirect competitors, DIY/manual solutions, and the do-nothing option (status quo bias).\n\nDIMENSION 6: Why Current Solutions Fail\nFor each solution, identify functional, emotional, economic, or friction failures.\n\nTHE VERDICT\nChain-of-Thought reasoning, then:\nDemand Status: [Strong/Moderate/Weak/False Positive]\nConfidence Level: [High/Medium/Low]\nCritical Adjustments Required: [Success requirements or pivot suggestions]\nRed Flags to Monitor: [2-3 indicators that would invalidate this analysis]\n\nDistinguish \"vitamin\" vs. \"painkiller.\" Question your own assumptions explicitly. Prioritize depth over breadth.",
